From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dsound: effects on the buffer format, LOCDEFER status, channel fallback

Effects (SetFX) and the groups dsound8's tests had marked todo_wine:

- SetFX offers the effect the buffer's own format (PCM or float, the sub
  format of an extensible one, sample size = block align) instead of 32-bit
  float; the effects therefore run on the buffer's data before it is converted
  for the device: the mixer copies the next source frames of a buffer with
  effects, runs IMediaObjectInPlace::Process on the copy and mixes from it (the
  application's buffer is not modified).
- Result codes are untouched on an invalid call, DSFXR_UNKNOWN for an effect
  that is not registered or refuses the type (DMO_E_TYPE_NOT_ACCEPTED), and a
  failed SetFX removes the effects set before.
- GetStatus of a DSBCAPS_LOCDEFER buffer reports no location until
  AcquireResources or Play.
- Channel layouts without a dedicated mapping (mono to other layouts, for
  instance 8 or 3 channels, stereo to 8, 6 to 4 ...): the channels both sides
  have are copied one to one (mono feeds the front pair) and the device's other
  channels are silent, instead of "falling back to stereo" with garbage in the
  remaining channels; the FIXME is gone.
- A WAVEFORMATEXTENSIBLE with another sub format is DSERR_INVALIDPARAM (the
  documented answer): the FIXME on it became a warning, as did the FIXMEs on the
  unknown IID of QueryInterface (E_NOINTERFACE).

